  "body": "## What\n\nThe second Fort Dearborn's blockhouse gets the cupola its own pictures draw, and loses the\ninvented chimney that was standing in its place. **This is a bounded partial increment of\nT-2388** \u2014 the ticket's all-buildings, all-pictures acceptance is NOT met and the ticket is\nreleased OPEN with the remaining differences recorded.\n\nPanel 5 of the Kurz & Allison sheet of 1893, captioned \"Fort Dearborn as rebuilt 1835\", draws\nthis blockhouse with a small square body at the centre of its four-sided cap, under a little\nfour-sided cap of its own, and draws no stack anywhere on that roof. The two Wau-Bun\nreproductions of the 1831 view (`kinzie_1857_chicago_1831_panorama`) draw the same body. That is\nwhat is now built.\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| before | the invented brick stack at the apex |\n| after | the pictured cupola, seated into all four roof planes |\n\n`docs/RESEARCH/second-fort-cupola-T-2388/` holds both, rendered through `photo_match.mjs` from\n**one identical camera** with nothing changed between them but the blockhouse's own bytes\n(`4b49f0db\u2026` \u2192 `96d9fb80\u2026`), beside the panel itself.\n\n## Why, and what is and is not claimed\n\n* **The cupola's OCCURRENCE is inferred** from the two identified pictures. Every dimension \u2014\n  the 1.8 m side, the 2.1 m body, the 0.22 m cap eave, the 36\u00b0 cap pitch, the 0.12 m seat, the\n  plain boarded sides with no louvres and no finial \u2014 is **reconstructed**, lives in the\n  archetype rather than the record, and is admitted in `docs/LIBERTIES.md`\n  \u00a7 `L-second-fort-blockhouse-cupola-2388`. A tier-5 retrospective chromolithograph supplies\n  form, never a metric, and its caption is not proof the feature stood on 1 July 1835.\n* **`chimneys: 0` is a choice about what to DEPICT, not a finding about heating.**\n  `_chimneys` stands its single stack at exactly the centre of the plan \u2014 the cupola's place \u2014\n  so the two could not both be built and one of them is pictured. The record says in as many\n  words that this is not a claim of no heating, no flue, or no later secondary projection, and\n  the stack has not been quietly moved somewhere else. The 1856 Kellogg/Blanchard print (filed\n  misleadingly as `chicago_fort_dearborn_river_mouth_1830.jpg`) depicts about 1836\u20131849 and does\n  show a louvred cap and an ambiguous projection beside it; that later detail is left\n  unresolved, not backdated.\n* **The join is real.** A box set down at the apex floats clear of the covering at its own\n  corners, because the pyramid falls away in every direction \u2014 a strip of sky, and somewhere to\n  hide a stack. The body's foot is carried 0.12 m below the lowest the main roof reaches\n  anywhere under its footprint, so it comes up through all four planes. The main roof is the\n  same four planes `_hip_roof` has always laid.\n\n## How\n\n* `fort_structure_params.py`: a keyword-only, **default-off** `cupola` field (added to\n  `CONSUMED`, read by `from_phase`), its five reconstructed dimensions as named module\n  constants, and validation that accepts **only the combination that is built** \u2014 a\n  `blockhouse`, a `pyramid` roof, and no separately generated centre stack \u2014 with every\n  dimension bounded and checked finite. Existing records and callers keep exactly their previous\n  semantics; nothing is turned on globally.\n* `fort_structure.py`: a local `_cupola` helper, called from `_building` only when the record\n  asks. **Not** the lighthouse's `lantern` (only `_tower` consumes that, so setting it on a\n  blockhouse would add nothing at all), not routed through the tower builder, no shared geometry\n  changed. `_hip_roof`'s own overhang is now a named constant so `_cupola` reads it instead of\n  copying the literal.\n* `data/structures/fort_dearborn_blockhouse.json`: `form.cupola` (inferred, with its sources and\n  reasoning), `form.chimneys` 1 \u2192 0 with the full admission, and the `roof_type` note corrected \u2014\n  it used to end \"no cupola is built here\".\n* The record keeps the `fort_structure(kind=blockhouse)` / `log_1816` phase, the surveyed seat\n  and 8\u00b0 rotation, the inferred 14.52 \u00d7 9.80 m footprint **and its \u00b125 % ambiguity**, the 5.2 m\n  reconstructed walls, two storeys, the 0.45 m jetty, loopholes, doors, main pyramid at 30\u00b0 and\n  every palette.\n\n## The 25-master family\n\nChanging the producer stales every `fort_structure` asset, so **all 25 current masters** \u2014 the\nalready accepted 1832 lighthouse and the Lake House construction shell included \u2014 were genuinely\nrebuilt on pinned **Ubuntu 26.04 / Blender 4.5.3** in two bounded native batches before the first\nsource commit. All 25 `inputs_sha256` in `assets/manifest.json` are the regenerated ones.\n**Exactly one master's bytes moved** \u2014 `fort_dearborn_blockhouse__log_1816.glb`,\n134,632 \u2192 133,092 \u2014 and its WEB derivative was re-encoded; the other 24 came back\nbyte-identical and keep their genuinely bound existing derivatives. No foreign registry row was\ntouched, and no other job's source, claims or branches were gone near.\n\n## The picture on the card\n\n`kurz_allison_1893` is cited by the record, which is what puts it on the Images tab through\n`compile_pictures.py`. `data/structure_grades.json` carries an explicit **pictured ruling**\nsaying why panel 5 is a reasonable whole picture of this named building, so the sidecar grade\nderives `attested` from the rule \u2014 not hand-typed, and **not** taken as a camera-fit shortcut:\nthe only camera on this panel is the T-3040 compound diagnostic, whose eye reached its imposed\n100 m bound, and the ruling says so.\n\n## Verification\n\n* `tools/check.sh --part 1/4`, `2/4`, `3/4`, `4/4` \u2014 **all four PASS**, every one a bounded\n  foreground run (part 1 re-run after `compile_source_use.py` rebuilt its backlinks). No gate\n  step reported a missing module.\n* `tools/compile_liberties.py`, `tools/compile_scene.py --all`, `tools/compile_source_use.py`,\n  `tools/changelog-entries.mjs --check`, `tools/publish.sh` \u2014 all clean.\n* Before/after compound comparison through `photo_match.mjs`, same camera, both committed.\n* Smoke: the parts `tools/smoke_budget.mjs --for-diff` names for this diff, at **1280\u00d7800 and\n  390\u00d7780**, reported in a comment below.\n\n## What is NOT claimed\n\nThe view's verdict is **`differs`** and `T-2388` is **released OPEN**. Still open on this\nbuilding's own picture: the camera is an unfitted 100 m diagnostic and is marked\n`diagnostic_only`; the galleried range's identity, the facade openings, the other roof forms and\nchimney counts, and the compound's whole composition are unresolved; and the other dated\npictures the ticket lists have not been read against the model at all. Only the roof assembly is\nmarked `fixed`. No new photo ticket, no split, no `done --pr`.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---\n\n*Opened in place of #1682, which was the same branch and the same work as a draft; the draft could not be made ready for review without a GraphQL mutation this runner does not spend, so it was closed and this one opened non-draft. The full verification is in the comment below, and `dev` has since been merged in \u2014 see the merge commit for how each conflict was taken.*\n",
